Review Text:
I really wanted to like this pump. I have been exclusively breast feeding and pumping from week #2. I started with a Medela manual pump and early on received the Medela Pump n Style ( through my insurance)- I was super happy with both of those Medela products.
When my baby was about 6- 7 months old,I felt my pump n style was slowing down or my milk flow was changing. I couldn't really figure it out so I decided to try the Sonata- which seemed awesome. I was going on a 2 week vacation overseas and it was the perfect time to get this pump because of the rechargeable battery. It worked really well for the first few months and I felt like it was pumping more milk in less time than my other pumps.
After 2 months of using my Sonata I noticed the milk was going into the air pipes (backflow) which was extremely frustrating. I rechecked all the components to make sure they were attached properly - to no avail. It was frustrating especially since I was at work and felt the pump was not getting out a lot of my milk and when it was,  a lot of it was getting wasted. SO in the end I do not recommend this pump- it looks beautiful and makes very little noise but turned out to be a &#34;let down.&#34;
